WEBVTT

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.270
ENUCLEATION CEREMONY

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.770
It's all my fault.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.110
If only...

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.820
I'd turned back then...

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.330
It's all because of me...

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:02.910
that he...

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.010
EPISODE 11:
DESPERATION, GOUT,
AND REBELLION

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.520
WHITE BLOOD CELL

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.520
CELL

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.770
<i>Hey! Good work!</i>

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.360
<i>Can't he hear us?</i>

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.830
Ugh! This is messed up!

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:05.780
You've got that right.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:10.370
The blood vessel's full of the waste products
it couldn't process.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:15.670
There's been even more greasy food
and alcohol lately, so no wonder.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.090
I'm sure it's all an outlet for stress,
but it's getting hard to take.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:24.470
He's totally not getting enough exercise.
Just look at that!

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.430
The place is teeming
with Fat Cells, too, huh?

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:30.600
<i>Fat Cells.</i>

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.980
<i>Cells that contain fat droplets
or what we call "oil."</i>

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.780
<i>They become enlarged with the consumption
of high-calorie foods and lack of exercise,</i>

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.990
<i>causing obesity.</i>

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.450
I know! We can't go on like this!

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:49.410
No days off for us,
and none of us are getting any sleep!

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.370
If we don't get any time
to take care of ourselves,

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.670
of course it's only going to make
our work environment worse.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.920
Seriously, what's going on
with this body anyway?

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.680
<i>Sleep deprivation.</i>

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:06.600
<i>The brain's waste products
are absorbed by the cerebrospinal fluid</i>

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.140
<i>and excreted into the bloodstream.</i>

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:12.850
<i>But since this activity increases during sleep,</i>

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:17.270
<i>prolonged sleep deprivation can lead
to the impairment of brain functions.</i>

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:20.900
<i>The discord among the cells is only growing.</i>

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.070
<i>I just hope it doesn't lead to trouble.</i>

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.200
<i>Emergency! Emergency!</i>

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.160
<i>Bacteria sighting reported!</i>

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.120
<i>White Blood Cells are to head
to the site immediately!</i>

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:35.080
<i>Repeat! White Blood Cells,
please head to the site immediately!</i>

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:41.090
An unknown bacterium has been detected
near the base of the left big toe!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.840
Here's a visual!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:45.550
What is this?

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.340
This is...

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:51.970
Senpai!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.810
Thank goodness we were able to catch up!

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:57.400
There's a pathogen at large.
They say it's in the left big toe.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.020
Why would it show up there, of all places?

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.030
You can look into that later.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.110
- Right!
- Right!

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:19.000
Could the left big toe be any farther away?

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.000
Wait, where are the germs?

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.340
Since we're in the foot,
could it be athlete's foot again?

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:27.470
Well, not that anything could surprise us now.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:38.100
Wh-What kind of germ is that?

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.820
It looks like really bad news!

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.130
Look at you, totally freaking out.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.780
Who wouldn't freak out over that thing!

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.160
That germ is gigantic!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.740
That one is definitely bad news!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.670
Don't you have any insight
at all on him, Memory Cell?

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.960
<i>Memory Cell.</i>

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:04.670
<i>A Lymphocyte that remembers
the immune responses of antigens.</i>

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:09.010
<i>When the same antigen invades the body,</i>

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:12.850
<i>they're prepared to trigger
accelerated antibody production.</i>

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.100
Nothing.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:15.600
Nothing here, either.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.690
Or here or there! It's all...

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:20.650
That's...

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.280
the first pathogen
that we've ever encountered!

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:27.030
First encounter... In that case...

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.990
Right. Our first order of business
should be to gather the data.

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.700
<i>White Blood Cells, phagocytose the target!</i>

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.700
<i>Macrophages, identify the antigen!</i>

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:36.660
Copy that!

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.000
Understood.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.130
Now then, let's go.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:48.720
<i>Phagocytosis.</i>

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:53.510
<i>The process by which White Blood Cells and the like
engulf bacteria and other foreign substances,</i>

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.310
<i>and break them down.</i>

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:56.890
No taste?

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:05.190
How awful. To think
that our attacks are ineffective...

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:08.150
It's no good! We can't acquire immunity!

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.610
We still can't identify the pathogen!

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.490
Now that it's come to this,
we'll have to do whatever it takes!

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:18.450
Everyone, Battle Formation One!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.410
Battle Formation One!

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.380
We've received a request
to get into Battle Formation One.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.130
Did you say "Battle Formation One"?

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:29.130
Meaning we're up against a bacterium
that powerful?

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:35.100
All units, head to the left big toe immediately!
And deploy reinforcements in the rearguard!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:40.060
Battle Formation One!
All units, head to the left big toe!

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.480
<i>If there's some collateral damage, so be it!</i>

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.520
<i>Break through no matter what!</i>

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.480
Battle Formation One, deployed!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.440
Battle Formation One has been deployed!

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:52.400
Commence full assault!

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:54.870
Fire!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.170
Hey, kiddo! You'd better make a run for it!

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:14.890
They say we're being attacked
by a new strain of bacteria!

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.680
Really, what's going on these days?

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:20.270
Oh my!

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:23.440
I wonder if he's okay.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.120
Hey, you there!

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.500
Hey, I'm talking to you!

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:49.590
You were with him the other day, weren't you?

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:56.260
<i>Hey there, aren't you going to stop by
for some tea today?</i>

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.890
<i>Hey, if there's ever anything
you want to grumble about, give me a holler!</i>

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.520
<i>My, my, how heartless!</i>

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.190
You know, I haven't seen him lately.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:12.570
He used to stop by all the time
and chat with me.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:18.820
Oh right, you're him, right?
His classmate, the honor student?

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.120
Huh?

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:26.040
He used to talk about you all the time.
You could see how proud he was of you!

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:30.210
<i>When work gets really tough
and all I want to do is bail,</i>

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.960
<i>I make myself think of him.</i>

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:37.220
<i>When I think, "Hey, he must be delivering oxygen
like the super straight arrow that he is,"</i>

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.550
<i>it gives me just enough energy
to dig in and work harder.</i>

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:44.980
<i>Well, I guess you could say
he's a friend I can trust.</i>

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:49.730
<i>No way would he ever betray me.
And I don't ever want to betray him, either.</i>

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:57.200
You can't just make friends
that you can trust, even if you want to.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.740
So, make sure you take care of him, all right?

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:02.990
I...

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:05.290
couldn't take care of him.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:06.250
What?

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:08.750
I...

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:10.750
Hey you!

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.930
SPLEEN

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:19.930
<i>The spleen.</i>

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:24.810
<i>About the size of a fist,
it's a spongy and soft organ.</i>

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.810
<i>It's made up of White Pulp and Red Pulp.</i>

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:34.190
<i>Red Blood Cells, please line up, proceed
through the gate and undergo your screening.</i>

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.740
This is as far as you're going.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:45.790
All right.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.210
<i>Red Pulp.</i>

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:53.340
<i>Filters the blood
and removes unneeded material.</i>

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:56.460
<i>In addition, it monitors
the Red Blood Cells' condition,</i>

00:10:56.460 --> 00:11:03.300
<i>sorting out abnormal, old or damaged cells
that can no longer function.</i>

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.520
Thank you so much
for all your hard work until now.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:20.570
<i>Aside from sorting blood and sending it
to the muscles when needed,</i>

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:24.370
<i>the spleen's other functions include producing
mature B Lymphocytes and T Lymphocytes,</i>

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:29.290
<i>and destroying the Red Blood Cells
sorted by the Red Pulp.</i>

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:34.750
<i>Red Blood Cells, do not stop. Please keep moving.</i>

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:42.550
What's the matter? Keep going.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.140
Please process me.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.890
I can't work anymore.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:54.310
A cell who can't work doesn't deserve to live.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.110
Please...

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.190
process me.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.450
You're still young...

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:05.570
and you're not malfunctioning in any way.

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:07.280
Get back to work.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:11.620
Do you hear me? Get back to work.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:14.920
Because of me...

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.880
Because of me, a friend of mine died.

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.420
Even though he trusted me.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:25.800
I just wasn't the guy he thought I was.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.560
I betrayed him.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:32.230
I'm a useless cell who isn't fit to live!

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:35.940
I'm begging you.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:40.110
J-Just end things for me, please!

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.610
Please...

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.780
put an end to me.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.620
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:58.130
This isn't a place
where the useless get processed!

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.170
It's where the curtain goes down

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:03.300
on the lives of the Red Blood Cells
who've carried out their duties to the end!

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.550
And it's my job to determine who they are!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.430
Somebody died because of you?

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.350
You're useless?

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.430
Who do you think you are?

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:18.270
You have a long way to go
before you can find purpose in your job!

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.780
Get up! Get up on your feet and move on!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.940
Work! Cell!

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.990
Work!

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:40.040
Due to the battle with the unknown pathogen,
there are signs of inflammation everywhere!

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.300
At this rate, the damage is only going to spread
to the surrounding areas!

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.260
What the cell are we supposed to do?

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:49.050
Um, there's something
that's been bothering me.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:49.760
What is it?

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:54.140
Suddenly showing up in a strange spot
like the base of the big toe...

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.520
Keeping even its infiltration point from us...

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:00.730
Is there a cell capable of such a thing?

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:04.320
Meaning it didn't come from outside.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.820
Then, where the cell did it come from?

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.700
What's this displaying?

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:11.660
It's a graph showing
the uric acid levels in this area.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:15.370
Uric acid? But these levels are...

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:19.040
Yes. They've been hovering
around the danger zone for days now.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.750
<i>Uric acid.</i>

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:25.460
<i>A waste by-product formed
during the breakdown of purines,</i>

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:31.100
<i>the energy substance produced in the body
when food is consumed or metabolized.</i>

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:35.390
<i>It is particularly insoluble in the bloodstream
of the extremities where the body temperature is low,</i>

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:38.940
<i>such as the lower torso and fingertips,
and is conducive to buildup.</i>

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.230
Uric acid.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.400
A mysterious pathogen.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.530
I see! So, that's what it is!

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.530
What is it?

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:50.610
He's...

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.990
No, I mean that thing is no pathogen.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:54.740
What?

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:57.960
Unscathed.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.540
Seriously?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.170
<i>We know what it is!</i>

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:04.130
<i>It's uric acid that didn't get dissolved
in the bloodstream</i>

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.760
<i>and ended up crystallized as urate.</i>

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:09.260
Crystallized uric acid?

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:12.600
Uric acid is a purine metabolite.

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:16.930
When there's excess purine intake
due to gorging, uric acid levels soar,

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:22.150
and we've been mistakenly attacking
that urate crystal as a pathogen.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:25.860
We've actually triggered gout!

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:30.070
<i>Gout.</i>

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:33.820
<i>Occurs when uric acid, a waste product
in the bloodstream, forms sharp crystals.</i>

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:40.920
<i>When these are attacked by White Blood Cells,
inflammation ensues, causing severe pain.</i>

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:43.710
<i>As pain can be triggered
merely by a gust of wind,</i>

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:47.300
<i>it came to be known as "painful wind."</i>

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.880
Then,

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.430
that means that, in trying to protect this body...

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.850
we've actually been abusing it instead?

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.980
I-I don't believe this.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.320
What does it matter?

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.200
Unless we inflict this much damage,

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:15.280
this body will never hear our cries.

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.740
Rookie?

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:22.250
No matter how hard we work, it's useless.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.830
We have to change this body.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:32.220
Open your eyes, dammit!

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:37.560
Do something about this work environment,
or there'll be no turning back!

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.020
Stop gorging on food and drink!
Stop smoking, too!

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:43.600
Get enough sleep!

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.400
Exercise, dammit!

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:46.480
He's right!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.440
How the cell...

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.110
How the cell can we work
under these conditions?

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.070
Give us more vitamins!

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:55.530
Let us rest once in a while!

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:57.910
You're consuming too much nicotine!

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.990
Cut back on the alcohol!

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.290
Knock it off.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:13.590
Come on, enough already!

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:17.220
Knock it off!

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:18.720
I said knock it off!

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.760
Please don't stop me!

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:27.940
You're absolutely right.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:31.280
But what good will this do?

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:37.320
There's nothing else that I can do anymore.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:42.330
All I can do is make an appeal
to this body like this.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:45.620
I know.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.500
No matter how hard we work,

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:50.880
unless this body changes,

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:54.050
this code black environment
will never change!

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:56.260
That's why we're all suffering.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.680
I know only too well how you feel.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:03.720
I don't know how many times
I've lost hope for this body myself.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:05.850
In this world...

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:11.270
cells are born and die
at a breakneck pace.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.280
We may all be different...

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:18.820
but we're all here to protect this body
and to carry out our tasks.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.120
What we need to do as the ones left behind

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:30.380
is to keep this body going. The body
that our dear friends risked their lives to protect.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.460
Not destroy it.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.840
Let's take better care of it.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:42.970
This world that our friends put their lives
on the line to protect...

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.350
And you yourself, as well...

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.320
It wasn't your fault that he died.

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:56.030
See? You forgot these.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.950
Don't blame yourself anymore.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.080
Don't try to shoulder the load by yourself.

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:10.250
<i>Don't try to shoulder the load by yourself.</i>

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:24.010
<i>Please hear it.</i>

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.140
<i>Us cells crying out...</i>

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:31.900
<i>This body has reached its limit!</i>

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:40.110
The White Blood Cells have ceased their attacks
on the urate crystal and have settled down.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.200
The ingested coichicine
appears to be working.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:45.830
<i>Coichicine.</i>

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:53.710
<i>Inhibits microtubule polymerization
by binding to a protein called "tubulin,"</i>

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:58.510
<i>inhibiting White Blood Cell activity,
leading to an anti-inflammatory effect.</i>

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:01.130
<i>Used to treat gout.</i>

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:05.010
<i>As prolonged use can cause damage
to reproductive organs,</i>

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:07.140
<i>it must be taken with caution.</i>

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:11.390
Even if we've suppressed
White Blood Cell activity,

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:15.610
nothing will change unless the purine levels
decrease and the uric acid levels go down.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:20.320
But if this kind of inflammation keeps
recurring, it's going to be grim.

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:23.780
Aren't the naturally-supplied purines
going to decrease?

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:25.660
I don't know.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:29.160
Can this body stop neglecting
its health after all these years?

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:33.750
And I really hope that the damage from all that
drinking and smoking will come to a stop.

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:42.050
<i>The risk of a gout attack increases
when the blood uric acid level rises above 7 mg/dL,</i>

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.720
<i>and this state continues
for several years.</i>

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:48.640
<i>Female hormones can induce
the flushing out of uric acid,</i>

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:52.060
<i>and so, 90% of gout patients are male.</i>

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:57.270
This is how close to the edge
this body's been driven by psychological stress.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:02.860
I wonder who the real villain is here.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.670
Come on, rookie! Run! Run!

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:16.880
You're never going to be done at this rate!

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:18.500
I'm sorry!

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:23.670
Jeez, we're even more understaffed than ever.
What the cell can we do?

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:26.470
The blood vessels are deteriorating
by the day, too.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.890
Whoa!

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:34.230
And it's going to be a while
before the rookies will be of any use.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.820
Oh my gosh! The oxygen!

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:46.450
Hey! What are you doing?

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:21.500
PREVIEW

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:22.750
Man, you really had me worried!

00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:23.750
RETURN

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:26.420
To think that the coronary artery
could get completely clogged like this...

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:27.340
THE HEART

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:27.720
This condition is...

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:28.420
Ah, ah...

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:29.470
DEMISE

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:34.010
We will now hold an emergency
meeting for all cells.

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:34.010
RETURN, THE HEART, AND DEMISE
